<title>SWEDEN: Iceland airport May cargo volumes fall 11 pct.</title>
<headline>Iceland airport May cargo volumes fall 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iceland's international airport at Keflavik handled 1,737 tonnes of freight in May, down 11 percent from the same month a year earlier, Iceland's civil aviation administration said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The administration published the following figures about airport activity for the month.</p>
<p>						    May 1997	May 1996</p>
<p>KEFLAVIK INT'L AIRPORT</p>
<p> Cargo export (in tonnes)			1,062	   1,281</p>
<p>	 import					  675	     671</p>
<p> Total						 1,737	   1,952</p>
<p> Mail export (in tonnes)			    45		37</p>
<p>	import					   112	     116</p>
<p> Total						   157	     153</p>
<p> Passengers					 92,256	  83,286</p>
<p>-- Klas Bergelind, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
